  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Five on the run – fill the lanes off the rebound",
  "description": "Five players, no defence. The coach (or a player) shoots and the centre E grabs the rebound. E pivots to the sideline and passes straight out to the guard A, who has moved to the sideline at free-throw-line height. A dribbles to the middle and up the floor. The wings B and C sprint along their sidelines, D runs straight to the other basket and E follows as the trailer.\n\nAt the other end A passes to a wing who drives and lays it in. D is on the block ready for the rebound and E stops at the top. The next group of five starts when the first is over half-court. Change positions every time and run it from both sides.\n\nVariations: finish with a pass to D on the block, or let E get the ball at the top for a shot. Demand that the ball is over half-court in three dribbles or fewer. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The rebounder turns to the sideline straight away – the outlet must go before the defence can close."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The guard meets the outlet with their back to the sideline and eyes up the floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wings run wide on the sideline and deep to the corner – that creates space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "All five move at once: nobody waits to see what happens."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
